From 00a8e5668a5518b430a58e62e8b448fab1ca9354 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:59:43 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] rpmsg: qcom_smd: Keep failed channel registration retryable

qcom_smd_create_device() can fail allocating or registering the RPMsg
device.
The state worker ignores its result and marks the channel registered
anyway.
A later worker pass then skips the still-closed channel because registered
is true, although no device exists. Registration cannot recover on that
channel through subsequent state work.

Set registered only after successful device creation, while holding the
channels lock. A later state-work invocation can retry a failed creation.
Successful registration, including a device awaiting its consumer driver,
retains its existing behavior. Other channels continue to be processed.

A host model executes the actual worker with synthetic channel lists,
registration failures and endpoint close/reopen services. Its 788 cases
reproduce 11 failed assertions before this change and pass afterward. Four
clean behavioral controls reject lost failure handling, registration state,
close recovery and the local RPM-only edge policy. Native ARM/ARM64 normal
and RT builds pass with no new diagnostics; inherited RPMsg documentation
warnings remain. These do not qualify real kernel concurrency or hardware.

Codex found the issue and generated the fix, host model and this draft
message during the Fx0 recovery audit. Public source history verifies the
initial ignored result and unconditional registration assignment. Human
review and DCO remain pending. Nothing has been submitted.

Fixes: 53e2822e56c7 ("rpmsg: Introduce Qualcomm SMD backend")

Backport to the maintained 6.18.63 Fx0 integration. Original integration
model evidence remains separate. In the combined three-fix series, the
relevant focused model passes 396 cases. The complete series also compiles
on ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT with nonpermissive CFI. ARM32 RT is unsupported
in this maintained kernel and is not counted as an RT build.

Codex prepared this local backport and its verification. Human review
and DCO remain pending; the MPM issue also awaits human security
classification. Nothing has been published or sent to maintainers.

Backported from commit daba8b5e5d5c232b6674ca44a759aee692bcaba8 ("rpmsg:
qcom_smd: Keep failed channel registration retryable").
---
 drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c
index 75b3071bd093..3eaffa206615 100644
--- a/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c
+++ b/drivers/rpmsg/qcom_smd.c
@@ -1278,6 +1278,7 @@ static void qcom_channel_state_worker(struct work_struct *work)
 	struct rpmsg_channel_info chinfo;
 	unsigned remote_state;
 	unsigned long flags;
+	int ret;
 
 	/*
 	 * Register a device for any closed channel where the remote processor
@@ -1302,9 +1303,10 @@ static void qcom_channel_state_worker(struct work_struct *work)
 			continue;
 
 		spin_unlock_irqrestore(&edge->channels_lock, flags);
-		qcom_smd_create_device(channel);
+		ret = qcom_smd_create_device(channel);
 		spin_lock_irqsave(&edge->channels_lock, flags);
-		channel->registered = true;
+		if (!ret)
+			channel->registered = true;
 	}
 
 	/*
-- 
